<p>Hello hello! Not an official critter or anyone with any sort of authority, but I can still read and give my thoughts.<br />
And when reading this, they are pretty much two.</p>
<p>One, is that there isn't really&#8230; much to this, at all, I feel. It feels very much like a Series I object. Better yet, it feels like a 'thing that does a thing'. Yes, there is this alien object that orbits the sun and sucks up energy. So? Besides this idea probably having already been written, at least to some capacity- I'd have to check as this kind of skip isn't generally my thing- what story do you have to tell?</p>
<p>The central narrative sounds like what you'd expect from any SCP article where the object cannot be contained, aka the Foundation trying to remedy the effects of said object; what sets it apart? Nowadays, at least from what I see, people want more from their SCPs. They want a story. A narrative.</p>
<p>For instance, you could expand on where this alien object comes from; you say it is an 'alien base'. That implies to me there is an alien civilization that built it. Who are they? What do they want? Why did they build this?<br />
If it were me, given this framework, I'd have them build this station because they are running out of energy and will all die if they don't do this. This not only provides a narrative, but also introduces the ethical question for the Foundation of 'do we let them die to save ourselves'?</p>
<p>All in all, I recommend you expand your idea draft! There is potential to this idea, so I think you could get something interesting out of it.<br />
I hope this was helpful in some way!</p>

